{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n 'Car|Path|drive|Race|Camera|Renderer' Auto-Lap-Happy-Auto-Racing-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-041321/vendor/engine/API-INDEX.md | head -95\"","aggregated_output":"61:- 407 Renderer; r\n66:- 611 10e. Paths; E.Path: path\n93:- 1323 Module drive: cars on the ground plane, a race round a track, the drivers who race it (engine/modules/drive.js); E.Car: car, E.Race: race\n262:- `game.screen.filter = 'clean'` †: 'clean' | 'scanlines' | 'crt', drawn over the picture as it is presented, never on the buffer, and not under a test harness (navigator.webdriver). game.settings.fil [... omitted end of long line]\n407:## 9. Renderer\n463:- `new E.Game({ headless })`: no screen, renderer, sound or DOM input (tests, tools, a simulation in Node, where it is the default): scenes update and draw is skipped; drive it with advance() and inpu [... omitted end of long line]\n501:- `game.resetCamera()` †: undo setZoom and rotateView: the scene's own zoom again (camera.start, or camera.tall on a screen held upright; 1 without), no turn. The player's zoom stays (settings.zoom) [... omitted end of long line]\n514:- `game.start({ camera })`: a scene's { zoom: [.75, 2], start: 1, tall: 1.5, wheel: true }: the player zooms the camera within zoom (the wheel, - and =, a pinch, Settings, Camera zoom: theirs, kept, o [... omitted end of long line]\n611:## 10e. Paths\n613:- `new E.Path(points, o = {}) → path` †: new E.Path(points, { closed: false, smooth: null }): points [x, y, z] (z optional) or { x, y, z } (a side view's height is z); closed runs back to the first; s [... omitted end of long line]\n788:- `map.walkable(cx, cy)`: true where a body can walk: no wall and not a blocked floor (water, lava). Pathfinding uses this.\n1323:## Module drive: cars on the ground plane, a race round a track, the drivers who race it (engine/modules/drive.js)\n1325:- `new E.Car(o = {}) → car`: new E.Car({ x, y, angle, top, accel, brake, turn, grip, drift, kart, auto, surfaces, ground }): a car (the manual)\n1326:- `E.Car.collide(cars)`: bump every pair of cars that touch apart (equal weights, a little bounce)\n1344:- `new E.Race(o = {}) → race`: new E.Race({ path, laps, checkpoints, countdown, width, items }): a race round a closed path (the manual)\n1346:- `race.box(x, y)`: an item box at (x, y): a racer that drives through it gets an item (when it holds none)\n1347:- `race.drive(R, dt)`: a racer's way round: the intent race.update gives an AI racer's car (look ahead along the line, bends, overtakes, unsticking, the rubber band)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '407,452p' Auto-Lap-Happy-Auto-Racing-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-041321/vendor/engine/API-INDEX.md && sed -n '1323,1378p' Auto-Lap-Happy-Auto-Racing-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-041321/vendor/engine/API-INDEX.md && head -150 Auto-Lap-Happy-Auto-Racing-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-041321/vendor/engine/modules/drive.js\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '407,452p' Auto-Lap-Happy-Auto-Racing-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-041321/vendor/engine/API-INDEX.md && sed -n '1323,1378p' Auto-Lap-Happy-Auto-Racing-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-041321/vendor/engine/API-INDEX.md && head -150 Auto-Lap-Happy-Auto-Racing-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-041321/vendor/engine/modules/drive.js\"","aggregated_output":"## 9. Renderer\n\n- `r.H`: the screen's height in game pixels\n- `r.W`: the screen's width in game pixels\n- `r.actor(x, y, z, drawFn, o = {})`: Queue a character. drawFn(g, ox, oy) must draw with (ox, oy) as the projected position of world point (x, y, z). The engine adds outline, rim light, hit flash, afterimages and x-ray silhouettes. opts: {outline=true, rim=true, flash=false, alpha=1, xray=false, ghost:{color, life, alpha, owner}, hides, bias, every, key, emissive (it stays bright under lighting, as r.queue's)}\n- `r.actor({ xray })`: true shows the actor's hidden part (a translucent tint with a 1-px outline, r.xrayColor and r.xrayOutline; a checker in E.style.trans 'dither') wherever a wall, a prop or shape at least chest high, or anything queued with hides is drawn in front of it (not one rising less than E.HEIGHTS.level, 8, above its feet: the roof it stands on, a cut-down wall); xray: { color, outline (false: none), actors } picks the colors, and with actors: true other bodies drawn in front hide it too (a hero lost in a crowd keeps his shape)\n- `r.actor({ hides })`: true: this actor counts as an x-ray occluder even when no x-ray actor asked for actors\n- `r.actor({ ghost })`: ghost.owner (any {x, y, z}, usually the actor itself) keeps its afterimages sorted behind the live body\n- `r.actor({ every, key })`: every: n, key (any object, the character's own): its finished image is drawn again for n - 1 frames before drawFn runs again, at the place it is now (a background character animating at a lower rate, as classic games' townsfolk do: a phone's frame keeps the time for the ones that matter); not while it flashes, with a ghost, x-ray or GPU lighting\n- `r.actor({ wrap })`: [w, h], as r.sprite's: a world that wraps round shows the actor across each edge it crosses\n- `r.actorNow(x, y, z, drawFn, o = {})`: draw an actor at once, over what is drawn so far, not sorted by depth (a pass of the game's own: a body falling into a void painted over the level), with r.actor's options (outline, flash, alpha, ...)\n- `r.bh`: the buffer's height (H + 2)\n- `r.box(g, x0, y0, z0, x1, y1, z1, top, side)`: extruded box prop (crate, pedestal, table). Call inside a queue fn with its g.\n- `r.bw`: the buffer's width (W + 2: a pixel of margin each side for the sub-pixel camera)\n- `r.ctx`: the low-resolution buffer's 2D context: draw on it with E.px\n- `r.decal(fn, o)`: draw on the floor before the queue. opts.emissive (0..1) makes it glow under GPU lighting\n- `r.glowDisc(g, cx, cy, rad, color, a)`: glow halo from a cache: additive light rings (alpha style) or a dithered disc (dither style). a = 0..1 strength\n- `r.groundArc(x, y, r0, r1, a0, a1, color, alpha = 1, z = 0, g = this.tgt)`: a band of a ring on the ground from radius r0 to r1 and angle a0 to a1 (radians): melee telegraphs, sight cones\n- `r.groundDisc(x, y, rad, color, alpha = 1, z = 0)`: a dithered disc lying on the ground (radius in world units, z its height): shadows, auras, area attacks\n- `r.groundPts(x, y, rad, n = 18, z = 0)`: n screen points round a circle of radius rad on the ground at (x, y), height z: the outline of a ring or a fan\n- `r.groundRing(x, y, rad, color, alpha = 1, z = 0)`: a ring lying on the ground (radius in world units)\n- `r.marker(x, y, z = 0, o = {})`: an objective marker over a world point: a bobbing diamond (and its label) while it is on screen, an arrow at the screen's edge pointing to it while it is off (offscreen: false hides it then). o: { label, color: '#ffd040', offscreen: 'arrow' }\n- `r.overlay(fn)`: draw fn(g) on top of everything, in screen pixels (HUD, dialog, menus)\n- `r.pick(sx, sy)` †: what was drawn under a screen point (the HUD's pixels: input.clicked(), input.pointer()) in the last frame, front to back: the pick values of the actors, sprites, props and queued draws given one (r.actor(x, y, z, fn, { pick: unit })), each where its pixels went (an actor's drawn bounds; others' box, or a body's size round its point). [] for none\n- `r.ppu` †: pixels per world unit on the ground here: the view's scale times the zoom (iso 1.41, the others 1.5, overhead 1, at zoom 1). Rigs, maps and props grow with it; a sprite's pixel is a screen pixel at zoom 1 unless drawn with world: true\n- `r.prop(name, x, y, z, o = {})` †: set dressing from E.prop: r.prop('torch', x, y, z, { size, color, flip, light: true, halo: true, bias, hides, footprint }) feet on the world point; flames animate and glow. light: true also adds a warm light to game.lights. A prop at least chest high (E.HEIGHTS.chest, 22: a pillar, a statue, a lamp) drawn in front of an x-ray actor shows the actor's silhouette through it; a lower one (grass, a crate, a barrel) doesn't; hides: true or false says so.\n- `r.queue(x, y, z, fn, o)`: queue a depth-sorted draw. fn(g) draws into g. opts: {bias, occluder, hides, xray, emissive, solid (hides a glow behind it), footprint, box, top} occluder: a wall (x-ray silhouettes show through it, it sorts as a block). hides: only lets x-ray silhouettes show through it (props, sprites, bodies), nothing else changes. box: [x0, y0, x1, y1], what it covers in buffer pixels: an occluder joins the x-ray only where its box meets a silhouette (without one, a 48 x 140 box round its foot: give a long wall its box, or queue it with queueSpan); top: its top's height (one under the knees hides nothing). It sorts by its one point (x, y, z): a long thing that other things stand along sorts wrong somewhere: queueSpan\n- `r.queueSpan(a, b, z, h, fn, o = {})` †: queue a long piece of geometry (a wall, a fence, a roof's edge, drawn whole by fn(g)) a cell at a time from a to b ([x, y] world units) at height z, h tall: each cell-long piece sorts at its own middle, clipped to its part, with its box (as the engine's own walls are). o: queue's options, depth (its thickness across, 0), step (16 units)\n- `r.shadow(x, y, rad, alpha = .5, color = '#0c0818', z = 0)`: soft contact shadow under a character: a cached dithered ellipse, correct for the current view. z = height of the surface it falls on (0 = floor; the top of a block or platform otherwise)\n- `r.shape(id, x, y, z = 0, o = {})` †: Queue a shape standing at (x, y, z), feet on the point, depth sorted like an actor: r.shape(id | entry, x, y, z, o). o: { facing (radians, where its front points; default PI/2, south, as written), scale, mats: { slot: material }, flip (mirror it x to -x before facing), params (a generator's: { h: 30 }), bias, hides (x-ray silhouettes show through it: by default when it stands at least E.HEIGHTS.chest, 22, high), footprint, light (add its lights to game.lights), shadow (default true), charView (default true: steep views draw it from the characters' lower angle), flash, alpha, xray, pick (r.pick finds it) }\n- `r.sightCone(obs, o = {})` †: an observer's view on the ground: a dithered fan fov wide (radians) about its facing, out to range, cut short where the map hides a body's chest (map.ray, the height rules), draped over the ground below. o: { range: 120, fov: 1.6, facing, map, eye, color: '#ffe080', alpha: .3, rays }. Call it in draw (it is a decal: under walls and bodies)\n- `r.sky(colors, o = {})`: background of dithered color bands, top to bottom: r.sky(['#0b1030', '#3b2d6b', '#e0806a']). Call first in draw.\n- `r.sprite(x, y, z, spr, o = {})`: Queue a pixel sprite (from E.sprite) standing at world point (x, y, z). Depth sorted like an actor. opts: { flip, anchor: 'bottom' (feet on the point, default; E.shapeSprite's: its own feet) | 'center' | 'top', glow: 0..1, bias, flash, outline, alpha, xray, ghost (the last five use the actor path), t (an E.anim's clock: spr may be one), rot (radians, about its center: anchor 'center' unless given), steps (16), scale, world: true (it grows with the view's scale, as rigs and maps: r.ppu pixels a unit), wrap: [w, h] (a world that wraps round: a copy across each edge it crosses; w alone wraps x) }\n- `r.starfield(o = {})`: scrolling star dots for space and night skies. opts: { count: 70, speed: 30 px/s, dir: 'down' | 'up' | 'left' | 'right', colors, layers: 3, seed }\n- `r.text(str, x, y, color = '#ffffff', o)`: HUD text in screen pixels, drawn on top and never lit: r.text('SCORE 120', 4, 4, '#fff', { align, scale, outline })\n- `r.textAt(x, y, z, str, color = '#ffffff', o = {})`: text floating at a world point (names, prompts): r.textAt(x, y, z, 'OPEN', '#ffe08a')\n- `r.tgt` †: current draw target for ground helpers (switches during GPU info and overlay passes)\n- `r.view`: the view this frame is drawn in (the game's, with zoom and turn)\n- `r.visible(x, y, z = 0, mx = 60, up = 30, down = 90)`: is a world point near the visible area? margins in pixels (characters extend upward from their feet)\n- `r.w(x, y, z = 0)`: world -> buffer pixel coords\n- `r.game`: its game; items: this frame's queue (sorted by depth when the frame ends)\n- `r.glowMask = true` †: false lets emissive glows show over everything under canvas lighting (cheaper: the default keeps walls and bodies in front of a glow dark)\n- `r.gpu = false` †: true during a frame drawn with GPU lighting (draw code can check r.gpu)\n- `r.ix`, `r.iy`: the camera's whole-pixel offset this frame (a world point is at r.w(x, y, z) on the buffer)\n- `r.outline = '#140c1c'`: the color of the 1-pixel outline round every actor\n- `r.rim = '#ffe2b8'` †: the rim light's color on actors' lit edges\n## Module drive: cars on the ground plane, a race round a track, the drivers who race it (engine/modules/drive.js)\n\n- `new E.Car(o = {}) → car`: new E.Car({ x, y, angle, top, accel, brake, turn, grip, drift, kart, auto, surfaces, ground }): a car (the manual)\n- `E.Car.collide(cars)`: bump every pair of cars that touch apart (equal weights, a little bounce)\n- `car.boost(sec = .8, power = .4)`: a boost: seconds of it, power (.4: top speed up by that share)\n- `car.spinOut(sec = 1)`: spin out (a shot, a hazard): seconds without control, most of its speed lost\n- `car.update(dt, map, c = {})`: one step: steering, engine, grip, drift, the surface, then E.Body's walls and hop. c: an input or an intent\n- `car.airT = 0`: a hop's seconds in the air\n- `car.angle`: its heading\n- `car.boostT = 0`: a boost's seconds left\n- `car.bumped = false`: it hit a wall or a car this step\n- `car.charge = 0`: a kart's drift boost building (1 blue, 2 orange)\n- `car.drifting = 0`: -1 left, 1 right, 0 not\n- `car.o`: its options\n- `car.offroad = false`: on a surface that slows it\n- `car.onGround = false`, `car.vz`: E.Body's (a hop leaves the ground)\n- `car.slide = 0`: sideways\n- `car.speed = 0`: along it (units a second, - backing up)\n- `car.spinT = 0`: a spin-out's\n- `car.surface = null`: the floor tag under it\n- `car.vx`, `car.vy`: its speed on the ground (E.Body's): along its heading and the slide\n- `new E.Race(o = {}) → race`: new E.Race({ path, laps, checkpoints, countdown, width, items }): a race round a closed path (the manual)\n- `race.add(car, o = {})`: a racer: its car, o.name, o.input (a player's controls) or o.ai ({ skill, rubber, lane }); returns it\n- `race.box(x, y)`: an item box at (x, y): a racer that drives through it gets an item (when it holds none)\n- `race.drive(R, dt)`: a racer's way round: the intent race.update gives an AI racer's car (look ahead along the line, bends, overtakes, unsticking, the rubber band)\n- `race.grid(n)`: the start: n places behind the line, two by two, facing along it: [{ x, y, angle }]\n- `race.hud(r, R, o = {})`: the standard HUD for a racer, in its viewport: place, lap, time, item, the countdown, WRONG WAY, FINISH (o.color; o.right: the x its right-hand text ends before, clear of a corner button)\n- `race.update(dt, map)`: one step: the countdown, every car, bumps, items, progress, laps, wrong way, places, the finish\n- `race.use(R)`: fire a racer's item: boost (now), shot (ahead along its heading), hazard (behind it)\n- `race.boxes = []`, `race.hazards = []`, `race.shots = []`: the items on the track\n- `race.go = false`: racing (the countdown over)\n- `race.o`: its options\n- `race.over = false`: every racer finished\n- `race.path`: the racing line\n- `race.racers = []`: every racer, in the order added\n- `race.results = []`: the racers as they finished\n- `race.t`: seconds since GO (- before it)\n\n## Module fight: one-on-one fighting: fighters with frame data, guards, throws, specials, a meter; rounds; a CPU; training (engine/modules/fight.js)\n\n- `E.FIGHT_KEYS: up, down, left, right, lp, hp, lk, hk, start, pause, confirm, cancel` †: the fighting preset (a scene's input): the moves and menu keys of E.Input.DEFAULT, light and heavy punch (U, I; a pad's X, Y), light and heavy kick (J, K; A, B)\n- `new E.FightAI(o = {}) → fightai` †: new E.FightAI({ level: 1..8 (4), seed }): a CPU for a fighter\n- `fightai.intent(f, foe, dt)` †: what it does this step: an intent for fighter f.update(dt, intent) ({ x, y: -1..1 on screen, press, do })\n- `fightai.level` †: how well it fights (1 to 8)\n- `fightai.react` †: seconds before it sees what its foe does\n- `fightai.rng` †: its own randomness (the seed's: the same match each time)\n- `new E.FightSelect(game, o = {}) → fightselect` †: new E.FightSelect(game, { roster: [{ id, name, rig, about }], inputs: [p1, p2 or null], cpu: [false, true], seed, onDone: ids => {} }): a character select\n- `fightselect.draw(r)` †: draw the roster, the cursors and each side's fighter large\n- `fightselect.update(dt)` †: move the cursors, take the picks; onDone(ids) once both have one\n- `fightselect.at` †: each side's cursor\n- `fightselect.cpu` †: which sides the CPU picks for\n- `fightselect.game` †: the game it runs in\n- `fightselect.inputs` †: each side's E.Input\n- `fightselect.o` †: its options\n- `fightselect.picks = [null, null]` †: each side's id once chosen\n- `fightselect.rects = null` †: where each portrait was drawn ([x, y, w, h] in screen pixels: a tap there picks it)\n/*!\nmy-3D2dge module DRIVE v0.89.1: cars on the ground plane, a race round a track, the drivers who race it\nhttps://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge (MIT License)\nLoads after: the full engine or the agent edition. Needs: no other module.\n\nSuper Mario Kart's, F-Zero's, Micro Machines' and GTA's cars: speed along the heading, a slide sideways that grip\ntakes away, the floor's tag under it slowing it, walls and other cars it bounces off; a race round a line of points.\n- const car = new E.Car({ x, y, angle, top: 240 (units a second), accel: 200, brake: 380, turn: 2.4 (radians a second\n  at speed), grip: 10, drift: 4.5 (the grip drifting), kart: true (a hop into a drift; held, it charges a boost),\n  surfaces: { grass: { top: .5, grip: .9 }, sand, dirt, ice, boost: { boost: .8 } (seconds), ... }, ground: (x, y) =>\n  tag (else map.floorAt) }): an E.Body. Each step car.update(dt, map, game.input (steer left/right; gas, brake, drift:\n  actions; o.auto: gas by itself) or an intent { steer: -1..1, gas, brake (0..1), drift (held), top (a factor) }).\n- car.speed (along it), car.slide (sideways), car.angle, car.drifting (-1, 0, 1), car.charge (a drift's: 1 blue, 2\n  orange), car.boostT, car.surface, car.offroad, car.spinT; car.boost(seconds, power), car.spinOut(seconds);\n  E.Car.collide(cars) bumps them apart.\n- const race = new E.Race({ path: a closed E.Path (the racing line; the full engine's), laps: 3, checkpoints: 8, countdown: 3, width: 40\n  (the track's half: the drivers' lanes), items: ['boost', 'shot', 'hazard'] }); race.grid(n) -> the start places\n  [{ x, y, angle }]; race.add(car, { name, input (a player's) | ai: { skill: .95, rubber: .2 } }) -> a racer { car,\n  name, lap, place, prog (distance raced), times, best, finished, time, wrong, item }.\n- Each step race.update(dt, map): the countdown (race.go once it says GO), every car driven (players by their input,\n  the rest by race.drive(racer): look ahead along the line, brake for bends, overtake, unstick, rubber band), bumps,\n  laps through the checkpoints in order (a shortcut counts nothing), wrong way, places, the finish (race.results, then\n  race.over); race.box(x, y) an item box; race.use(racer) fires a racer's item; race.shots, race.hazards to draw. The\n  3D engine's vehicles (world.vehicle) race as cars do: pass race.update a null map; Rapier bumps them.\n- race.hud(r, racer, { color, right }): the place, the lap, the time, the item, the countdown, WRONG WAY and FINISH (in its\n  viewport; right: the x its right-hand text ends before).\n\n```js drive\nconst E = My3D2dge, map = new E.TileMap({ w: 30, h: 30 }), car = new E.Car({ x: 40, y: 40, angle: 0 });\nfor (let i = 0; i < 240; i++) car.update(1 / 120, map, { gas: 1 });\nif (!(car.speed > 150 && car.x > 150 && Math.abs(car.y - 40) < .01)) throw new Error('a car accelerates along its heading');\n```\nRules: the angle is a heading (0 east, PI / 2 south) and a mode7 camera's; update cars at the fixed step; a player's\ncar takes game.input or its player's input; race.update moves every racer's car, so don't update them yourself.\n*/\n(function (E) {\n'use strict';\nif (!E) throw new Error('my-3D2dge module DRIVE: load engine/my-3d2dge.js (or the agent edition) first');\n\n/* =============================================================================\n * DRIVE  cars, races, drivers\n * ========================================================================== */\nconst { clamp, angDiff } = E, TAU = Math.PI * 2;\nconst SURFACES = { grass: { top: .5, grip: .9 }, sand: { top: .4, grip: .6 }, dirt: { top: .7, grip: .8 }, ice: { grip: .15 }, boost: { boost: .8 } };\nclass Car extends E.Body {\n  /** new E.Car({ x, y, angle, top, accel, brake, turn, grip, drift, kart, auto, surfaces, ground }): a car (the manual) */\n  constructor(o = {}) {\n    super({ x: o.x || 0, y: o.y || 0, z: o.z || 0, r: o.r || 7, h: o.h || 14, bounce: o.bounce === undefined ? .3 : o.bounce });\n    /** o: its options */\n    this.o = Object.assign({ top: 240, accel: 200, brake: 380, reverse: 70, turn: 2.4, grip: 10, drift: 4.5, drag: .5, hop: 110, kart: false, auto: false }, o);\n    this.o.surfaces = Object.assign({}, SURFACES, o.surfaces);\n    /** angle: its heading; speed: along it (units a second, - backing up); slide: sideways; drifting: -1 left, 1 right,\n     *  0 not; charge: a kart's drift boost building (1 blue, 2 orange); boostT: a boost's seconds left; spinT: a\n     *  spin-out's; surface: the floor tag under it; offroad: on a surface that slows it; bumped: it hit a wall or a car\n     *  this step; airT: a hop's seconds in the air */\n    this.angle = o.angle || 0; this.speed = 0; this.slide = 0; this.drifting = 0; this.charge = 0; this.boostT = 0; this.spinT = 0; this.surface = null; this.offroad = false; this.bumped = false; this.airT = 0;\n    this._boostK = 0; this._hopDir = 0; this._stall = 0;\n  }\n  /** a boost: seconds of it, power (.4: top speed up by that share) */\n  boost(sec = .8, power = .4) { this.boostT = Math.max(this.boostT, sec); this._boostK = Math.max(this.boostT > sec ? this._boostK : 0, power); return this; }\n  /** spin out (a shot, a hazard): seconds without control, most of its speed lost */\n  spinOut(sec = 1) { if (this.spinT > 0) return this; this.spinT = sec; this.vx *= .3; this.vy *= .3; this.drifting = 0; this.charge = 0; return this; }\n  /** one step: steering, engine, grip, drift, the surface, then E.Body's walls and hop. c: an input or an intent */\n  update(dt, map, c = {}) {\n    const o = this.o, inp = typeof c.move === 'function';\n    let steer = inp ? c.move()[0] : c.steer || 0, gas = inp ? (c.down('gas') || o.auto ? 1 : 0) : c.gas || 0, brake = inp ? (c.down('brake') ? 1 : 0) : c.brake || 0;\n    const drift = inp ? c.down('drift') : !!c.drift, hop = inp ? c.pressed('drift') : drift && !this._held;\n    this._held = drift;\n    const tag = o.ground ? o.ground(this.x, this.y) : map && map.floorAt ? map.floorAt(this.x, this.y) : null, S = (tag && o.surfaces[tag]) || {};\n    this.surface = tag; this.offroad = (S.top || 1) < 1;\n    if (S.boost && this.onGround) this.boost(S.boost);\n    if (this.spinT > 0) { this.spinT -= dt; this.angle += 11 * dt; steer = 0; gas = 0; brake = .5; }\n    if (this.boostT > 0) { this.boostT -= dt; gas = 1; }\n    const air = !this.onGround;\n    // a kart hops on the drift button; landing still steering, it drifts that way while held, charging a boost\n    if (o.kart) {\n      /** vz, onGround: E.Body's (a hop leaves the ground) */\n      if (hop && !air && this.spinT <= 0) { this.vz = o.hop; this.onGround = false; this._hopDir = Math.sign(steer); }\n      if (!air && !this.drifting && drift && this._hopDir && this.speed > o.top * .4) this.drifting = this._hopDir;\n      if (this.drifting) {\n        if (!drift || this.speed < o.top * .2) { if (this.charge >= 1) this.boost(this.charge >= 2 ? 1 : .55, .35); this.drifting = 0; this.charge = 0; this._hopDir = 0; }\n        else this.charge += dt * (steer * this.drifting > 0 ? 1.5 : .8);\n      }\n      if (!drift) this._hopDir = 0;\n    } else this.drifting = drift && Math.abs(this.speed) > o.top * .3 ? Math.sign(steer) || this.drifting : 0;   // a car's handbrake\n    // it turns with its speed (none standing, reversed backing up), harder into a drift, less in the air\n    const k = clamp(Math.abs(this.speed) / (o.top * .25), 0, 1) * Math.sign(this.speed || 1), turn = this.drifting ? this.drifting * .6 + steer * .4 : steer;\n    this.angle += turn * o.turn * k * dt * (air ? .5 : 1);\n    // its speed along the new heading and across it, from the world's\n    const fx = Math.cos(this.angle), fy = Math.sin(this.angle);\n    let v = this.vx * fx + this.vy * fy, s = this.vy * fx - this.vx * fy;\n    const top = o.top * (S.top || 1) * (c.top || 1) * (this.boostT > 0 ? 1 + this._boostK : 1);\n    if (gas > 0 && v < top) v = Math.min(top, v + o.accel * gas * (this.boostT > 0 ? 2.5 : 1) * dt);\n    else if (v > top) v = Math.max(top, v - o.accel * 1.6 * dt);   // over this ground's top: it slows to it\n    if (brake > 0) v = v > 1 ? Math.max(0, v - o.brake * brake * dt) : Math.max(-o.reverse, v - o.accel * .6 * brake * dt);\n    if (!gas && !brake) v *= Math.exp(-o.drag * dt);\n    if (!air) s *= Math.exp(-(this.drifting ? o.drift : o.grip) * (S.grip || 1) * dt);   // grip takes the slide away\n    /** vx, vy: its speed on the ground (E.Body's): along its heading and the slide */\n    this.vx = fx * v - fy * s; this.vy = fy * v + fx * s;\n    super.update(dt, map);\n    if (this.hitWall) { const f = Math.cos(this.angle), g = Math.sin(this.angle); this.vx -= f * Math.max(0, this.vx * f + this.vy * g) * .4; this.vy -= g * Math.max(0, this.vx * f + this.vy * g) * .4; }\n    this.speed = this.vx * fx + this.vy * fy; this.slide = this.vy * fx - this.vx * fy; this.bumped = this.hitWall; this.airT = air ? this.airT + dt : 0;\n    return this;\n  }\n  /** bump every pair of cars that touch apart (equal weights, a little bounce) */\n  static collide(cars) {\n    for (let i = 0; i < cars.length; i++) for (let j = i + 1; j < cars.length; j++) {\n      const a = cars[i], b = cars[j], dx = b.x - a.x, dy = b.y - a.y, d = Math.hypot(dx, dy), R = a.r + b.r;\n      if (d >= R || d < 1e-6 || Math.abs(a.z - b.z) > 10) continue;\n      const nx = dx / d, ny = dy / d, push = (R - d) / 2, vn = (b.vx - a.vx) * nx + (b.vy - a.vy) * ny;\n      a.x -= nx * push; a.y -= ny * push; b.x += nx * push; b.y += ny * push;\n      if (vn < 0) { const J = -vn * .65; a.vx -= nx * J; a.vy -= ny * J; b.vx += nx * J; b.vy += ny * J; }\n      a.bumped = b.bumped = true;\n    }\n  }\n}\nclass Race {\n  /** new E.Race({ path, laps, checkpoints, countdown, width, items }): a race round a closed path (the manual) */\n  constructor(o = {}) {\n    if (!o.path) throw new Error('E.Race needs { path }: a closed E.Path along the track (the racing line)');\n    /** o: its options */\n    this.o = Object.assign({ laps: 3, checkpoints: 8, countdown: 3, width: 40, items: ['boost', 'shot', 'hazard'] }, o);\n    /** path: the racing line; racers: every racer, in the order added; t: seconds since GO (- before it); go: racing (the\n     *  countdown over); over: every racer finished; results: the racers as they finished; boxes, shots, hazards: the\n     *  items on the track */\n    this.path = o.path; this.racers = []; this.t = -this.o.countdown; this.go = false; this.over = false; this.results = []; this.boxes = []; this.shots = []; this.hazards = [];\n  }\n  /** the start: n places behind the line, two by two, facing along it: [{ x, y, angle }] */\n  grid(n) {\n    const out = [], w = this.o.width * .45;\n    for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) { const p = this.path.at(-14 - i * 22), a = p.angle, side = i % 2 ? 1 : -1; out.push({ x: p.x - Math.sin(a) * w * side, y: p.y + Math.cos(a) * w * side, angle: a }); }\n    return out;\n  }\n  /** a racer: its car, o.name, o.input (a player's controls) or o.ai ({ skill, rubber, lane }); returns it */\n  add(car, o = {}) {\n    const d = this.path.nearest(car.x, car.y), L = this.path.length;\n    const R = { car, name: o.name || 'CAR ' + (this.racers.length + 1), input: o.input || null, ai: o.input ? null : Object.assign({ skill: .95, rubber: .2, grip: 520, lane: ((this.racers.length * .37) % 1) * 2 - 1 }, o.ai), lap: 0, cp: Math.floor(d / L * this.o.checkpoints) % this.o.checkpoints, place: this.racers.length + 1, prog: d > L / 2 ? d - L : d, _d: d, times: [], best: null, lapT: 0, finished: false, time: 0, wrong: false, _wrongT: 0, item: null, _stuck: 0, _back: 0 };\n    this.racers.push(R); return R;\n  }\n  /** an item box at (x, y): a racer that drives through it gets an item (when it holds none) */\n  box(x, y) { this.boxes.push({ x, y, t: 0 }); return this; }\n  /** a racer's way round: the intent race.update gives an AI racer's car (look ahead along the line, bends, overtakes,\n   *  unsticking, the rubber band) */\n  drive(R, dt) {\n    const car = R.car, P = this.path, ai = R.ai, v = Math.max(40, car.speed), look = 30 + v * .4, L = P.length;\n    // overtaking: a car just ahead in its lane moves it to the other side\n    for (const Q of this.racers) if (Q !== R) { const dd = Q.prog - R.prog; if (dd > 0 && dd < 70 && Math.abs(this._lane(Q) - ai.lane) < .5) { ai.lane = ai.lane > 0 ? -.6 : .6; break; } }\n    const p = P.at(R._d + look), off = ai.lane * this.o.width * .55, tx = p.x - Math.sin(p.angle) * off, ty = p.y + Math.cos(p.angle) * off;\n    const diff = angDiff(car.angle, Math.atan2(ty - car.y, tx - car.x));\n    // the sharpest bend ahead (its turn a unit along the line) and the speed it allows; faster than that, it brakes\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_18","type":"agent_message","text":"The title draw selected **Auto Lap Happy**. The original manual confirms five courses, four handling profiles across five colours, automatic acceleration, and pursuit points for crashes or a clear lead. I’ve split out world art, audio, and networking so I can focus on driving, checkpoint validation, and mode flow.\n"}}
