{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_43","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > PROGRESS.md <<'EOF'\n# Progress — Auto Lap Happy\n\n## Delivery\n- Title selected with \"'`secrets.randbelow` from 50 privately generated candidates (index 24).\n- Dev folder: `Auto-Lap-Happy-Auto-Racing-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-041321/`\n- Root HTML: `Auto-Lap-Happy-Auto-Racing-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-041321.html`\n- Root report still to finish: `exit-interview.json`.\n\n## Implemented\n- Pinned full my-3D2dge v0.89.1 at 8ecc2f62353761187bdfe226f327b7ea5d2eb691; unchanged AI Hub session client1.4.0 at35a1047f2067b2af3de3943f0fe452f39105d869.\n- Original five-course connected countryside; all five car bodies/four profiles; 12 directed gates/course; connectors, lake causeway, route navigation graph, hidden acceleration straight, passport.\n- Root authoritative fixed1/120 sim in src/sim.js. E.Car with reverse0/no negative brake creep. Ordered forward gates/local projection; all incident priority; checkpoint exchanges; trial2/5laps;10/50point pursuit;free drive;6stage guided tour;valid best records/ghosts separated from dev.\n- Native shaded pixel renderer: E.SHAPES bodies, wheels, landmarks, trees; road/corner arrows; flags/lean/skids/splash/dust. Fullscreen HTML TV-size UI; keyboard/pad/touch;settings;pause;dev sliders;credits pages;attract.\n- Code-only audio; music .10 default; engine/tyres/SFX/gibberish. Offline render tested Chromium and WebKit.\n- Direct WebRTC offer/answer UI with true gathered ICE, versioning, reliable/unreliable channels; authoritative network adapter and AI Hub shared-world. Protocol/input/snapshot tests.\n- Build command: `node tools/build.mjs` from dev folder emits index.html and exact root final artifact.\n\n## Tests/evidence so far\n- `node tools/test.mjs core`:52/52 pass after fixing meadow closure, AI passing lanes, tour navigation; includes25legal course/car laps, five-lap event, scored duel, full six-stage tour, directed gates/handling/incident priorities/snapshot/native draw.\n- Audio:13checks in each Chromium/WebKit,26/26.\n- Network:16unit+21real RTC loopback+21fileURL passed.\n- Official actual-game Hub harness:all5cases pass `complete` + `__hubCheck.pass` (solo,two players,150ms/50jitter/5%loss,host leave,actorless server). Agent network owns ongoing changes to online authority pump in app.js so online clock/hiddenhost remain monotonic independently of clipped render dt.\n- UI agent `/root/audio` rerunning actual root final browser suite after4UIissues fixed:device prompts,settingsfocus,devfocus,touch-attractclickconsumption. All screenshots under evidence.\n- Agent `/root/network` running actual invitation/reply/driving/scoring/rematch test tools/network-game-test.py; coordinating authoritypump fix.\n\n## Active architecture/contracts\n- src/world.js: HappyWorld;courses,path/samples/gates,width;surface/solids/routeBetween.\n- src/render.js: HappyRenderer(game,world),update/draw;no authoritative mutation.\n- src/sim.js: HappySim;start/step/snapshot/applySnapshot;HappyRules.DEFAULTS/PROFILES/TOUR/project/crossGate.\n- src/audio.js: HappyAudio lazy unlock,setVolumes,setScene,update,cue,gibberish,destroy.\n- src/network.js: HappyNetwork callbacks onStart/onInput/onSnapshot/onFinish/onEnd/onTimeUp. localSeat0/1/null,clock()sec. update sends throttle field (sim uses gas). Packed snapshots <1200 bytes.\n- src/app.js: UI orchestration; window.__happy read/testbridge guarded online; game.debug snapshot.\n- tools/test.mjs:quiet one entry filters core/audio/network/hub/ui/direct/package/all. Must integrate agent actual UI network script name (`network-game-test.py`) before final all.\n\n## Remaining work\n1. Complete monotonic online pump and rerun affected tests; agents report outcomes.\n2. Full input-driven browser tour and final actual-file smoke/WebKit/credits visuals; enhance any missing tutorial mechanical exposure.\n3. Final research/provenance, architecture/authoring/testing/issues docs, root README and complete real exit-interview JSON.\n4. Rebuild final bundled HTML with report;run comprehensive one-command checks against final artifact, JSON/package verify;update this log.\n5. Final chat MUST include Source Information,Testing Feedback,Engine Feedback,Prompt Feedback with every required answer; link final HTML and report. No unconfirmed hardware/internet claims.\n\n## Known issue ledger pending consolidation\nWorld agent:W1carfacing(visualmedium);W2meadowclosurecritical;W3boathouseplacementlow;W4gatetargetmedium.\nNetwork review fixes:rematchguard,oldroundpackets,missingremoteinitialbrake,disconnectbrake,finishsnapshot. Actual testing pump pacing exposed online clock issue.\nUI agent:UI01prompts,UI02settingsfocus,UI03devfocus,UI04touchdemoexit. Core tour test exposed same-lane AI train preventing points;passinglanes fixed52/52.\nNo current known core failures. Keep unique issue counts factual;don'\"'t count test assertion float tolerance as product bug.\nEOF\ncat > Auto-Lap-Happy-Auto-Racing-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-041321/docs/research.md <<'EOF'\n# Reference research and provenance\n\nResearch performed before implementation, 2026-11-06. The game is an original interpretation; no source map or artwork is embedded in the game.\n\n## Source\n- Auto Racing, Mattel Electronics / Intellivision, 1980.\n- Original instructions: https://history.blueskyrangers.com/instructions/autoracinginst.html — read source manual. Confirmed five courses in difficulty order, automatic acceleration, side-button braking, checkpoint restarts, five solo laps, pursuit to50:opponent crash2/clear lead1. Car relative ratings55/65/75/90/90, tan and blue identical. Original directional steering versus revised car-relative steering. Grass,skidding,water and scenery affect driving.\n- Blue Sky Rangers history: https://history.blueskyrangers.com/mattelelectronics/games/autoracing.html — historical account and corrected steering chronology,connected region/hidden drag strip reference. The original history page and manual are archived locally in docs/manual.html and docs/history.html.\n- Inspected the archival gameplay still \"'`AutoScreen.gif` from the history page: a tiny overhead single-seat car,green landscape,wide pale-grey road,angular bends,geometric orange-roof buildings. Inspected contemporary catalogue illustration `AutoCatPic.gif`: red open-wheel racer. These reference images remain in docs only,not in the packaged game. Source-owned reference material is not relicensed.\n- Found archival gameplay listings https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CmvZWlng-no and https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ffTKTX-9Nrk. Video playback/audio was not inspectable here. Exact source sound/music and detailed original track measurements:unknown. Manual web edition contains no map image; its text and history still informed the game. No video observation is claimed.\n\n## Original design additions\nThe new five circuits and all road geometry are authored independently. A guided six-stage tour,AI drivers,personal ghosts,hold-to-recover,short preset,route passport,manual throttle,touch assist and network transport are new features. No weapons,powerups,nitro,damage upgrades or currencies.\n\n## Dependencies inspected and pinned\n- my-3D2dge full handoff0.89.1,commit8ecc2f62353761187bdfe226f327b7ea5d2eb691: https://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge/tree/8ecc2f62353761187bdfe226f327b7ea5d2eb691/dist/handoff . Read README,complete API card,asset contract,drive module manual and KART kit. Native E.Car,Path,Game,SHAPES,materials/renderer and fixed-step system are used. MIT upstream notices preserved;vendor engine unchanged.\n- AI Hub Session Protocolv1 client1.4.0,commit35a1047f2067b2af3de3943f0fe452f39105d869: https://github.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/tree/35a1047f2067b2af3de3943f0fe452f39105d869/lib/hub . Read README,shared-world arena lifecycle,official harness and session client. Released session.js inlined byte-for-byte except safe closing-script escaping,first script immediately after charset. No custom external transport is constructed in a Hub session.\n- WebRTC primary references: https://webrtc.org/getting-started/peer-connections ; https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/RTCPeerConnection/createDataChannel ; https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/RTCPeerConnection/icegatheringstatechange_event . Non-trickle gathered SDP invitation/reply with real data channels. Public cross-NAT/TURN connectivity:unknown.\n\n## Licensing\nUpstream engine/header notices retained in full;original game source and procedural assets:MIT. No external runtime bitmap,font,audio or CDN dependency. Vendor package includes optional asset sets but the game uses only native core shapes and original definitions. Historical page/images are research evidence only,attributed to their owners.\nEOF'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
