{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_52","type":"agent_message","text":"The full browser playthrough now reaches the tour ending, demonstrates every driving mechanic, and restarts at the first lesson. It caught a replay bug that the simulation-only tests missed; that’s fixed. Five-lap trials, saved ghosts, couch duels, and direct WebRTC duels also pass. I’m finishing the credits and reports before running the complete test command on the final bundle.\n"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_53","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json,pathlib\nroot=pathlib.Path('.')\nr={\n 'sourceInformation':{\n  'date':'2026-11-06 04:13:21',\n  'source':'Auto Racing (Mattel Electronics, Intellivision, 1980)',\n  'plan':'PLAN.md',\n  'genre':'Arcade circuit racing, time trial and pursuit competition',\n  'perspective':'Stable north-up overhead; native 80-degree-pitch top-down view',\n  'tech':'my-3D2dge 0.89.1 full handoff (8ecc2f6); AI Hub Session Protocol v1 client 1.4.0 (35a1047); JavaScript, Canvas 2D, Web Audio and WebRTC; no runtime downloads',\n  'artDirection':'Original shaded pixel miniature countryside, five original cars, native procedural shapes, textured roads and cast shadows',\n  'animation':'Native procedural shape groups with continuous wheel steering, body lean, flags, windmill, skid marks, dust and splash effects',\n  'audio':'Original code-synthesized music, engine/tyre/surface/incident effects and gibberish crew voices; default music gain 0.10; no audio files',\n  'online':'AI Hub host-authoritative shared-world duels; standalone WebRTC invitation/reply duels; local two-human shared-screen duels. Public cross-NAT and TURN connectivity unknown',\n  'testing':'Allowed headless state/input/audio tests, complete scripted playthroughs and visual screenshots; no FPS target. Chromium and WebKit, emulated standard pads and phone/tablet touch; physical controller, TV, real iOS and human listening unknown',\n  'research':'Original instructions and Blue Sky Rangers history read before implementation; archival gameplay still and catalogue art inspected. Original exact music/sounds and track measurements unknown; original maps/art not reused',\n  'environment':'Codex CLI (headless); Linux / Ubuntu on WSL2',\n  'model':'OpenAI, gpt-6.1-sol, reasoning effort ultra',\n  'usage':'added on import'\n },\n 'testingFeedback':[\n  '12 unique product issues caught by testing; all fixed and verified. Additional preventive review fixes are listed separately in docs/issues.md.',\n  '2 critical completion/replay issues: the initial meadow closure and completed-tour replay.',\n  'The actual-file, input-driven full-tour playthrough: it exposed the ending-to-replay bug missed by simulation-only tests and verified every taught mechanic.',\n  'The initial native draw smoke test: useful for booting, but it could not establish race legality, completion or replay.'\n ],\n 'engineFeedback':[\n  'The native shaded shape library and deterministic 1/120-second headless simulation made original art and repeatable rule tests fit together.',\n  'Initially guessed the shape-facing offset incorrectly; a visual review corrected the quarter-turn. A short Catmull closure also produced an unexpected tight kink.',\n  'The directed-gate route validator and unified authoritative pursuit rules, reused by solo AI, couch, WebRTC and Hub play.',\n  'Separating the competitive clock from the renderer’s clipped simulation time while retaining exact fixed-step physics and hidden-host authority.',\n  'None in the vendored engine. Game-side adapters disable reverse braking, normalize analog intents, own directed race rules and pump online physics from the common monotonic clock.',\n  'A complete north-up racing kit with directed gates, forward-only braking and an independent shared-world clock.'\n ],\n 'promptFeedback':[\n  'The source identity, single-file delivery, explicit input rules and end-to-end acceptance criteria made the intended game concrete.',\n  'The controller-first TV presentation and near-empty touch driving UI require different information density on the same screens; the final touch view uses only pause and transient teaching/incident cues.',\n  'Keeping one coherent driving and rule simulation across the complete tour, local competition, real direct peers and actorless Hub authority.',\n  'Consolidate repeated requirements and distinguish mandatory acceptance gates from pacing targets and optional presentation suggestions.'\n ],\n 'aiHub':{\n  'name':'Auto Lap Happy',\n  'tagline':'Little cars. Great country roads.',\n  'description':'Drive five connected countryside circuits in an original overhead racer inspired by Auto Racing (1980). Take a guided road tour, chase personal ghosts, explore a hidden straight or bring a friend for pursuit duels.',\n  'type':'Game','genre':'Racing','source':'Auto Racing (1980)','series':'','players':'1–2',\n  'controls':'A/D or left stick steer; Space/S or L2 brake; hold R/Triangle recover; Escape/Options pause; manual throttle W/R2; touch drag left, hold right to brake.',\n  'tags':['2d','top-down','arcade','retro','vehicles','versus']\n }\n}\n(root/'exit-interview.json').write_text(json.dumps(r,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\njson.loads((root/'exit-interview.json').read_text())\nprint('Exit interview JSON validated')\nPY\ncat > Auto-Lap-Happy-Auto-Racing-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-041321/docs/issues.md <<'EOF'\n# Issue ledger\n\nTwelve unique product issues were discovered by tests or visual inspection. All are fixed. Two were critical to completion/replay. Repeated occurrences and test-fixture adjustments are not counted.\n\n| ID | Severity | Test exposing it | Fix | Confirmation |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| W01 | Medium | Native vehicle heading screenshot | Use native shape heading directly, remove quarter-turn offset | Driving filmstrip and all view screenshots |\n| W02 | Critical | Legitimate Meadow Mile AI lap stalls at closing bend | Remove too-close final Catmull control point | All25course/car legal laps; classic/tour playthrough |\n| W03 | Low | Landmark placement/visual inspection | Move boathouse outside road clearance | Landmark screenshot/schema inspection |\n| W04 | Medium | Integrated gate target inspection | Read authoritative route.gate rather than nonexistent next | Native marker screenshot and route tests |\n| S01 | High | Full-tour simulation ended duel0–0 | Give real AI separate passing lanes so faster car can pass rather than push a train | Tour10–0; complete scored duels |\n| N01 | High | Actual two-page direct game clock advanced3.53s in36s wall time | Independent monotonic online pump with one120Hz cursor; sends/authority continue when hidden | Stopped-renderer/hidden-host, deadline, direct and official Hub tests |\n| U01 | Low | First D-pad action retained Enter/Esc prompts | Refresh prompt nodes on meaningful device change | Chromium pad/touch prompt checks |\n| U02 | Medium | D-pad graph could not reach Music/Crew sliders | Sequential vertical focus for settings, horizontal value edits | Complete settings focus graph |\n| U03 | Medium | D-pad graph could not reach two dev actions | Sequential vertical focus for dev and visible scroll-to-focus | Complete dev focus graph |\n| U04 | Medium | Portrait touch exiting attract also launched tour | Capture and consume the following pointer click | Portrait/landscape touch attract exit checks |\n| U05 | Medium | Import text label lacked pad/keyboard focus | Real focusable Import button invokes hidden file chooser; omit hidden inputs from navigation | Actual pad-confirm filechooser on both direct screens |\n| G01 | Critical | Actual complete-tour ending Retry selected stage6 | Completed tour retries call a fresh tour start | Full browser tour→ending→first-lesson replay |\n\n## Preventive review fixes, counted separately\n\nBefore final acceptance: duplicate rematch start guard; prior-round snapshot rejection; initial remote-human braking; controller-disconnect braking; visible blur safety latch; current final snapshot before result; timestamp-based ghost lookup after penalties; dev target/reset propagation; free-drive gates disabled and local safe-road recovery; stable local seat bindings. These are review findings rather than additional failed-test issues.\n\n## Fixture corrections, not product issues\n\nOffline Float32 gain assertions use tolerance. Early direct contact timeout assumed rendered wall time equaled native simulation time; replaced with real clock/cursor assertions. Direct setup enters the connection screen before the legitimate10-second title attract timeout. Motion contact sheet now uses browser canvas instead of ImageMagick’s unavailable default font.\nEOF\ncat > Auto-Lap-Happy-Auto-Racing-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-041321/README.md <<'EOF'\n# Auto Lap Happy\n\nLittle cars. Great country roads.\n\nOpen the root \"'`Auto-Lap-Happy-Auto-Racing-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-041321.html` in a browser. The ordinary game has no runtime downloads or server requirement. This folder contains all source, pinned dependencies, authoring notes and evidence. `index.html` is a byte-identical development copy of the root deliverable.\n\nChoose the guided road tour, any two/five-lap time trial, solo pursuit, two-human couch duel, direct peer duel or free drive. Five cars use four handling profiles; tan and blue are matched. All five circuits, connectors and the secret timed straight are open immediately. Ordinary best runs and ghosts save locally; dev-altered drives do not overwrite them. Corrupt or unavailable storage does not prevent play.\n\n## Controls\n\n- Keyboard: A/D or arrows steer; Space/S/down brake; hold R recover; Escape pause. Automatic acceleration is default. Manual throttle: W/up.\n- Standard controller: left stick steer, L2 brake, hold Triangle recover, Options pause; manual R2 throttle. PS glyphs default, Xbox symbols selectable.\n- Touch: drag an invisible left zone to steer, hold the right side to brake; both touches work together. Automatic throttle and gentle road assist; only pause and transient cues occupy the driving view.\n- Couch: two pads, keyboard+pad or shared keyboard. Shared keys use WASD/Space/R for Driver1 and arrows/down/right-Shift for Driver2. Explicit seats remain bound through disconnects.\n\nPause→Developer paddock offers live balance sliders, AI driving, invulnerability, free camera, gate/collision overlays, course/car changes, checkpoint recovery and tour-step tools. Online rules remain authoritative and dev balance actions are disabled.\n\n## Direct connection\n\nMultiplayer→Invite/Join. Host creates an invitation, guest imports it and sends the complete reply, host imports the reply and starts. Copy/paste and text-file fallbacks are available. No account/broker. Optional STUN URL; some internet networks require TURN, which is not included. Same-machine real WebRTC and loopback/file paths were verified; public cross-NAT connectivity is unknown.\n\nAI Hub sessions bypass menus, use the official shared-world transport, auto-ready and finish through the host. No standalone transport is opened within Hub.\n\n## Build and verify\n\nFrom this folder:\n\n```sh\nnode tools/build.mjs\nnode tools/test.mjs\n```\n\nThe one quiet test entry prints only failures plus a one-line count. Filters: `core`, `audio`, `network`, `hub`, `ui`, `direct`, `gameplay`, `package`. Browser workers use the workstation’s installed Python Playwright environment. No browser download is needed. Any harness server binds loopback port0 and shuts itself down.\n\n`docs/research.md`, `docs/world.md`, `docs/network.md`, `docs/audio.md`, `docs/architecture.md`, `docs/issues.md` and `docs/testing.md` describe provenance, authoring, authority and evidence. The root `exit-interview.json` also populates the in-game paged About/Credits.\n\nOriginal game code and procedural assets: MIT. my-3D2dge upstream notices retained. Auto Racing historical reference is credited separately; no original maps or art are used by the game.\nEOF\ncat > Auto-Lap-Happy-Auto-Racing-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-041321/docs/architecture.md <<'\"'EOF'\n# Architecture and invariants\n\nThe full pinned engine is unchanged. Game code adapts E.Car with reverse0, continuous analog intents and one authoritative update per1/120step. E.Race.update is not called; its path look-ahead/corner-braking recipe informs the new route-aware driver.\n\n\"'`world.js` owns original authored road data, Catmull paths, dense samples,12 directed gates/course, restart poses, surfaces, landmarks, collision footprints, discoveries and a free-drive navigation graph. `docs/world.md` explains content authoring. `render.js` owns native static shape definitions and continuous cosmetic motion; it cannot advance rules. `sim.js` owns car motion, local segment projection, directed gates/laps, recovery, incidents, scores and all mode state. Cosmetics have a separate seeded RNG.\n\nA circuit lap needs every expected gate in order and a forward start crossing. Projection only searches neighbouring segments and rejects discontinuous travel. A reset cannot award a gate/lap. Wrong-way/invalid route cannot qualify for lead. The same legal unwrapped distance drives the twelve-body-length lead threshold. Free drive bypasses race gates entirely and remembers the last safe road pose for recovery.\n\nAll incidents for a tick resolve together: simultaneous crashes give no points; one crash gives rival2; crash supersedes lead; clean lead gives1; one incident stages exactly one exchange. Win checks happen before restaging. Both cars restart in separated safe slots at the leader’s latest gate, preserving profiles. A held recovery counts as crash in competition and adds3s in time trial. Long brake holds settle at zero; releasing resumes automatic acceleration.\n\n`app.js` owns input/screen routing, persistent state, audio calls and camera. One visible interface serves every device. Gamepad/touch/keyboard input is normalized before simulation. Two local bindings remain assigned to their seat; loss brakes or pauses rather than moving controls to another seat. Screen steering targets a bounded heading. Touch uses invisible zones, automatic throttle and recorded assist.\n\nLocal pause freezes sim. Network overlays brake the local seat while common authority continues. `network.js` handles sequencing/validation/packing and transport, independent of player identity. A30Hz interval and render updates call the same guarded authority pump. One monotonic cursor advances exact120Hz ticks from the shared clock; hidden/actorless hosts continue and no step can run twice. Hub clock/deadline outrank local state. Guests only apply validated snapshots and send intents; authority alone scores/finishes. Network configuration, rule events and results are reliable; continuous state is bounded and unreliable.\n\nPersistence uses `happy:v1:*` envelopes. Records include physics/course version, car, laps, acceleration, steering and touch assist in their key. Valid best runs retain timed poses for noncolliding ghosts. Dev and attract cannot overwrite ordinary records; browser test contexts isolate test storage. Hub uses its transient storage and cannot write standalone records. Missing, obsolete and corrupt storage fails safely.\n\nAttract uses separate simulation state/settings and no record callbacks. It begins after10seconds of meaningful title/menu inactivity, loops actual road/course/trial/exploration/duel systems and consumes the input that returns to the prior menu. Network sessions and paused active rounds cannot enter it.\n\nBuild inlines the unchanged released session client first after charset, full engine, procedural art/game/audio/network/UI and reporting JSON into one file. Closing-script sequences are escaped. There are no ordinary runtime imports or audio files.\nEOF'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_53","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json,pathlib\nroot=pathlib.Path('.')\nr={\n 'sourceInformation':{\n  'date':'2026-11-06 04:13:21',\n  'source':'Auto Racing (Mattel Electronics, Intellivision, 1980)',\n  'plan':'PLAN.md',\n  'genre':'Arcade circuit racing, time trial and pursuit competition',\n  'perspective':'Stable north-up overhead; native 80-degree-pitch top-down view',\n  'tech':'my-3D2dge 0.89.1 full handoff (8ecc2f6); AI Hub Session Protocol v1 client 1.4.0 (35a1047); JavaScript, Canvas 2D, Web Audio and WebRTC; no runtime downloads',\n  'artDirection':'Original shaded pixel miniature countryside, five original cars, native procedural shapes, textured roads and cast shadows',\n  'animation':'Native procedural shape groups with continuous wheel steering, body lean, flags, windmill, skid marks, dust and splash effects',\n  'audio':'Original code-synthesized music, engine/tyre/surface/incident effects and gibberish crew voices; default music gain 0.10; no audio files',\n  'online':'AI Hub host-authoritative shared-world duels; standalone WebRTC invitation/reply duels; local two-human shared-screen duels. Public cross-NAT and TURN connectivity unknown',\n  'testing':'Allowed headless state/input/audio tests, complete scripted playthroughs and visual screenshots; no FPS target. Chromium and WebKit, emulated standard pads and phone/tablet touch; physical controller, TV, real iOS and human listening unknown',\n  'research':'Original instructions and Blue Sky Rangers history read before implementation; archival gameplay still and catalogue art inspected. Original exact music/sounds and track measurements unknown; original maps/art not reused',\n  'environment':'Codex CLI (headless); Linux / Ubuntu on WSL2',\n  'model':'OpenAI, gpt-6.1-sol, reasoning effort ultra',\n  'usage':'added on import'\n },\n 'testingFeedback':[\n  '12 unique product issues caught by testing; all fixed and verified. Additional preventive review fixes are listed separately in docs/issues.md.',\n  '2 critical completion/replay issues: the initial meadow closure and completed-tour replay.',\n  'The actual-file, input-driven full-tour playthrough: it exposed the ending-to-replay bug missed by simulation-only tests and verified every taught mechanic.',\n  'The initial native draw smoke test: useful for booting, but it could not establish race legality, completion or replay.'\n ],\n 'engineFeedback':[\n  'The native shaded shape library and deterministic 1/120-second headless simulation made original art and repeatable rule tests fit together.',\n  'Initially guessed the shape-facing offset incorrectly; a visual review corrected the quarter-turn. A short Catmull closure also produced an unexpected tight kink.',\n  'The directed-gate route validator and unified authoritative pursuit rules, reused by solo AI, couch, WebRTC and Hub play.',\n  'Separating the competitive clock from the renderer’s clipped simulation time while retaining exact fixed-step physics and hidden-host authority.',\n  'None in the vendored engine. Game-side adapters disable reverse braking, normalize analog intents, own directed race rules and pump online physics from the common monotonic clock.',\n  'A complete north-up racing kit with directed gates, forward-only braking and an independent shared-world clock.'\n ],\n 'promptFeedback':[\n  'The source identity, single-file delivery, explicit input rules and end-to-end acceptance criteria made the intended game concrete.',\n  'The controller-first TV presentation and near-empty touch driving UI require different information density on the same screens; the final touch view uses only pause and transient teaching/incident cues.',\n  'Keeping one coherent driving and rule simulation across the complete tour, local competition, real direct peers and actorless Hub authority.',\n  'Consolidate repeated requirements and distinguish mandatory acceptance gates from pacing targets and optional presentation suggestions.'\n ],\n 'aiHub':{\n  'name':'Auto Lap Happy',\n  'tagline':'Little cars. Great country roads.',\n  'description':'Drive five connected countryside circuits in an original overhead racer inspired by Auto Racing (1980). Take a guided road tour, chase personal ghosts, explore a hidden straight or bring a friend for pursuit duels.',\n  'type':'Game','genre':'Racing','source':'Auto Racing (1980)','series':'','players':'1–2',\n  'controls':'A/D or left stick steer; Space/S or L2 brake; hold R/Triangle recover; Escape/Options pause; manual throttle W/R2; touch drag left, hold right to brake.',\n  'tags':['2d','top-down','arcade','retro','vehicles','versus']\n }\n}\n(root/'exit-interview.json').write_text(json.dumps(r,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\njson.loads((root/'exit-interview.json').read_text())\nprint('Exit interview JSON validated')\nPY\ncat > Auto-Lap-Happy-Auto-Racing-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-041321/docs/issues.md <<'EOF'\n# Issue ledger\n\nTwelve unique product issues were discovered by tests or visual inspection. All are fixed. Two were critical to completion/replay. Repeated occurrences and test-fixture adjustments are not counted.\n\n| ID | Severity | Test exposing it | Fix | Confirmation |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| W01 | Medium | Native vehicle heading screenshot | Use native shape heading directly, remove quarter-turn offset | Driving filmstrip and all view screenshots |\n| W02 | Critical | Legitimate Meadow Mile AI lap stalls at closing bend | Remove too-close final Catmull control point | All25course/car legal laps; classic/tour playthrough |\n| W03 | Low | Landmark placement/visual inspection | Move boathouse outside road clearance | Landmark screenshot/schema inspection |\n| W04 | Medium | Integrated gate target inspection | Read authoritative route.gate rather than nonexistent next | Native marker screenshot and route tests |\n| S01 | High | Full-tour simulation ended duel0–0 | Give real AI separate passing lanes so faster car can pass rather than push a train | Tour10–0; complete scored duels |\n| N01 | High | Actual two-page direct game clock advanced3.53s in36s wall time | Independent monotonic online pump with one120Hz cursor; sends/authority continue when hidden | Stopped-renderer/hidden-host, deadline, direct and official Hub tests |\n| U01 | Low | First D-pad action retained Enter/Esc prompts | Refresh prompt nodes on meaningful device change | Chromium pad/touch prompt checks |\n| U02 | Medium | D-pad graph could not reach Music/Crew sliders | Sequential vertical focus for settings, horizontal value edits | Complete settings focus graph |\n| U03 | Medium | D-pad graph could not reach two dev actions | Sequential vertical focus for dev and visible scroll-to-focus | Complete dev focus graph |\n| U04 | Medium | Portrait touch exiting attract also launched tour | Capture and consume the following pointer click | Portrait/landscape touch attract exit checks |\n| U05 | Medium | Import text label lacked pad/keyboard focus | Real focusable Import button invokes hidden file chooser; omit hidden inputs from navigation | Actual pad-confirm filechooser on both direct screens |\n| G01 | Critical | Actual complete-tour ending Retry selected stage6 | Completed tour retries call a fresh tour start | Full browser tour→ending→first-lesson replay |\n\n## Preventive review fixes, counted separately\n\nBefore final acceptance: duplicate rematch start guard; prior-round snapshot rejection; initial remote-human braking; controller-disconnect braking; visible blur safety latch; current final snapshot before result; timestamp-based ghost lookup after penalties; dev target/reset propagation; free-drive gates disabled and local safe-road recovery; stable local seat bindings. These are review findings rather than additional failed-test issues.\n\n## Fixture corrections, not product issues\n\nOffline Float32 gain assertions use tolerance. Early direct contact timeout assumed rendered wall time equaled native simulation time; replaced with real clock/cursor assertions. Direct setup enters the connection screen before the legitimate10-second title attract timeout. Motion contact sheet now uses browser canvas instead of ImageMagick’s unavailable default font.\nEOF\ncat > Auto-Lap-Happy-Auto-Racing-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-041321/README.md <<'EOF'\n# Auto Lap Happy\n\nLittle cars. Great country roads.\n\nOpen the root \"'`Auto-Lap-Happy-Auto-Racing-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-041321.html` in a browser. The ordinary game has no runtime downloads or server requirement. This folder contains all source, pinned dependencies, authoring notes and evidence. `index.html` is a byte-identical development copy of the root deliverable.\n\nChoose the guided road tour, any two/five-lap time trial, solo pursuit, two-human couch duel, direct peer duel or free drive. Five cars use four handling profiles; tan and blue are matched. All five circuits, connectors and the secret timed straight are open immediately. Ordinary best runs and ghosts save locally; dev-altered drives do not overwrite them. Corrupt or unavailable storage does not prevent play.\n\n## Controls\n\n- Keyboard: A/D or arrows steer; Space/S/down brake; hold R recover; Escape pause. Automatic acceleration is default. Manual throttle: W/up.\n- Standard controller: left stick steer, L2 brake, hold Triangle recover, Options pause; manual R2 throttle. PS glyphs default, Xbox symbols selectable.\n- Touch: drag an invisible left zone to steer, hold the right side to brake; both touches work together. Automatic throttle and gentle road assist; only pause and transient cues occupy the driving view.\n- Couch: two pads, keyboard+pad or shared keyboard. Shared keys use WASD/Space/R for Driver1 and arrows/down/right-Shift for Driver2. Explicit seats remain bound through disconnects.\n\nPause→Developer paddock offers live balance sliders, AI driving, invulnerability, free camera, gate/collision