{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_78","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > docs/testing.md <<'EOF'\n# Acceptance evidence\n\nRun \"'`node tools/test.mjs` from this folder, or pass its full path. It prints failures and one final count. Browser workers return JSON to that entry point. Filters: `core`, `audio`, `network`, `hub`, `ui`, `direct`, `gameplay`, `package`. The comprehensive result is `evidence/test-all.json`.\n\n## Behaviour covered\n\n- Core simulation: all 25 car/course combinations finish legal laps; four profiles and matched tan/blue physics; analog pressure; countdown and long brake holds; surfaces; directed gates; wrong-way, missing gates, nearby roads, line oscillation and teleport rejection; incident priorities; safe recovery/exchanges; winning threshold and deadline draw; five laps; the full six-stage tour; connected navigation; discoveries; live tuning; snapshot restoration; native headless drawing.\n- Audio: 26 actual offline-render checks across Chromium and WebKit. Music, engines, tyres, effects and gibberish voices produce nonzero bounded signals. Initial music is exactly .10. Sliders, mute, pause, stop, destroy and repeated retries are measured.\n- Network adapter: 16 unit checks and 21 real RTC checks through each of file and loopback URLs. Complete gathered descriptions, two data channels, sequenced input/snapshots, 150 ms delay with 5% loss, malformed/truncated/wrong-type/incompatible descriptions, duplicate reply, old-round rejection, rematch and closure.\n- Hub: five official harness scenarios cover one/two humans, 150 ms latency / 50 ms jitter / 5% loss, host departure and actorless authority. Both `complete === true` and `__hubCheck.pass === true` are required. A live Hub round cannot construct a standalone transport.\n- UI: 56 actual root-file checks cover every menu’s controller focus graph, keyboard and pointing, PS/Xbox prompts, pad loss/reconnect, a controller-confirmed file chooser, dev sliders/reset/unranked state, exact attract boundary and consumed exits, save isolation, phone/tablet multitouch and cancellation, and WebKit file boot/driving/pause. Touch driving keeps only pause and transient teaching/incident cues visible.\n- Actual direct play: complete visible invitation/reply screens, text-file import and clipboard denial, contact, legal lead +1 and recovery/crash +2, target ten, both peers’ results, rematch, pause, hidden authority with renderer stopped, one monotonic 120 Hz cursor, exact common-clock deadline and closure. Delay/loss wraps real channels rather than a fake transport.\n- Actual game playthrough: 36 checks cover title → six guided stages → ending → first-lesson replay; real keyboard recovery, grass/gravel and water crash; every lesson flag; scored pursuit; classic five laps with five valid splits; versioned best/ghost and ghost retry; two-human couch separation → scored finish → rematch → title; no engine/browser errors.\n- Packaging: the unchanged official client is first after charset; root and development files match; runtime scripts and assets are inline with no audio files; metadata and all four reporting categories exist; the exit interview parses and has the exact required shape.\n\n## Visual evidence\n\nTitle, setup, race, phone/tablet, About/Credits, landmark and results screenshots were inspected. `motion-driving-filmstrip.png` shows car heading, wheel/lean motion and route clarity. State assertions establish legality and scoring; pictures do not substitute for actual driving.\n\n## Limits\n\nThe installed Chromium 153 and WebKit 26.6 use software rendering here. Controller and touch tests use standard-mapping stubs and phone/tablet profiles. Physical controller, TV, real iOS, human listening, a second person, public internet/cross-NAT connectivity and TURN coverage are unknown. Scripted-driver times are not claimed as a new player’s completion time. No FPS target or optimization gate was imposed.\n\nTwelve unique product issues, including two critical completion/replay bugs, were found and fixed. `docs/issues.md` records exposure, fix and confirmation. Preventive review fixes and fixture corrections are counted separately.\nEOF'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
